    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8124" root="حشم" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُشْمَةٌ</span></b>  (in the K, erroneously, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَشَمَةٌ</span>, TA):
see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَشَمٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also [in the CK, erroneously, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُشَمَة</span>]
<i>A woman,</i> or <i>a wife;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْأَةٌ</span>. (K, TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>I. q.</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذِمَامٌ</span> [app. as meaning <i>protection, safeguard,</i> or
<i>security of life and property</i>]. (Yoo, K.) So in
the phrase, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهُ الحُشْمَةُ</span> [<i>Protection,</i> &amp;c., <i>is due to
him</i>]. (Yoo, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>Relationship.</i> (K.) So in
the phrase, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِيهِمْ حُشْمَةٌ</span> [<i>Among them is relationship</i>]. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَشْمَةٌ</span>.

